  "question": {
    "text": "Suppose <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo></math>&nbsp;be an arithmetic progression of natural numbers. If the ratio of the sum of the first five terms to the sum of first nine terms of the progression is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>17</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>110</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>15</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>120</mn></math>, then the sum of the first ten terms of the progression is equal to"
  },
